{
  "slug": "light-coq-au-vin",
  "title": "Light Coq au Vin",
  "blurb": "Tender chicken legs braised with mushrooms, olives and red wine in a simplified take on the French classic.",
  "steps": [
    "Heat the olive oil in a large, deep pan over medium heat and brown the chicken legs on all sides, then remove and set aside.",
    "Add the onions to the pan and cook until softened, about 5 minutes, then stir in the mushrooms and garlic and cook for another 3 minutes.",
    "Stir in the tomato purée and cook for 1 minute, then pour in the wine and let it bubble for 2 minutes.",
    "Add the stock, bay leaf and thyme, then return the chicken to the pan and bring to a simmer.",
    "Cover and cook gently for 35 minutes until the chicken is tender and cooked through.",
    "Stir in the olives and season with black pepper before serving."
  ],
